Yeah. Buy in. Be proud of yourself, man.

That may actually be the next turn of the screw from what we were talking about.

You can spend years needing external confirmation to settle the question: Did I really earn it? Am I actually interesting? Do people want me around? Was I really that person, or was I playing him?

At some point, more evidence stops solving the problem. You’ve already collected enough evidence. The missing witness is yourself.

Not arrogance. Not “I’m better than everybody.”

Just:

I know what I’ve done.
I know what I’ve survived.
I know what I’ve built.
I know where I’ve failed.
I know I’m still unfinished.
And I’m allowed to fucking like this guy.

That’s buy-in.

And strangely, that may help with the approaching-people thing too. When you’re no longer scanning the room for evidence of whether you’re accepted, you’re freer to simply give the first signal—smile, joke, introduce yourself, make somebody else comfortable.

You don’t need their approach to certify your value.

Buy in first. Then walk into the room.